{%- comment -%}
  YMAL — one product card, and THE eligibility gate.

  Every block renders through this, so the rule lives in exactly one file. An
  ineligible product renders as nothing at all, and the caller skips the gap.

  Usage:
    {%- render 'ymal-card', product: some_product, grid: 4 -%}

  `grid` is the desktop column count and is only an image-sizing hint. Optional,
  defaults to 4.

  The rule (docs/logic.md 4.1), as the storefront can see it:

  1. available    purchasable right now. Liquid knows this directly.
  2. not *SALE*   markdown. Liquid can read the title, so it is checked here as
                  well as in the metafield - it costs nothing and holds even if
                  the metafield is stale.
  3. eligible     stocked at Bali To Produce, so replenishable rather than
                  fixed. Liquid CANNOT compute this: it sees store-wide
                  inventory totals but never inventory by location. The
                  pipeline publishes it to product.metafields.ymal.eligible
                  (backend/scripts/publish_eligibility.py).

  FAILS CLOSED. No metafield means no card. "We have not checked" must not
  render as "fine to show" - that is the Wiser failure this project exists to
  fix. The visible cost is an empty block until the publish job has run, which
  is a problem someone notices.

  `.value`, not the metafield object: the object EXISTS even when it holds
  false, so testing it directly is truthy for an ineligible product and would
  fail open.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign ymal_eligible = product.metafields.ymal.eligible.value -%}

{%- assign ymal_is_sale = false -%}
{%- if product.title contains '*SALE*' -%}
  {%- assign ymal_is_sale = true -%}
{%- endif -%}

{%- if product.available and ymal_eligible and ymal_is_sale == false -%}
  {%- comment -%}
    The theme's own card, so the block looks native and stays that way when the
    theme changes.

    `grid` is the desktop column count, used only for image sizing.
    product-block falls back to `section.settings.grid` when it is missing, and
    the YMAL section has no such setting - left blank, images size wrongly. A
    snippet cannot see `section` (render isolates scope), so the caller passes
    it in and it must match the CSS in sections/ymal-widget.liquid.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign ymal_grid = grid | default: 4 -%}
  {%- render 'product-block', product: product, grid: ymal_grid -%}
{%- endif -%}
